      SUBROUTINE ELIMTB (A,N)C     ELIMTB (A,N) WILL RETURN THE STRING <A> WHOSE LAST CHARACTER IS NOTC     BLANK. THE STRING RETURN WILL HAVE THE LENGTH N.C     THIS ROUTINE WILL FIND THE POSITION OF THE LAST NON-BLANK, ORC     TAB CHARACTER IN A AND RETURN THAT LOCATION IN N.      CHARACTER	A*(*)       NA = LEN(A)      IF (NA .LE. 0) THEN	N = 0	RETURN      END IF      IF (A .EQ. ' ') THEN        N = 0        RETURN      END IF      NA = LEN(A)      DO 10 100 I = NA, 1, -1      IF (ICHAR(A(I:I)) .EQ. 0) GO TO 10 100      IF ((A(I:I) .NE. ' ') .AND. (A(I:I) .NE. '	')) THEN	N = I	RETURN      END IF10100 CONTINUE      N = 0      RETURN      END